> **Attribution confidence:** HIGH requires a fanotify access immediately before physical I/O. MEDIUM is used only when exactly one process has a matching file/directory open at I/O onset. If multiple processes are plausible, the event remains UNKNOWN/ambiguous and is not credited to a process in wake-source statistics.
>
> Current-open-file snapshots and power/activity state files live under `/var/local/emhttp` (RAM). Wake history is the only persistent runtime data written to the boot device.

